+## 5. Baseline execution — run-id capture surface
+
+Run-id surface: SOP writes per-step artifacts under `.agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/`
+(`state.json`, `report.json`, `trace.json`, `metrics.json`, `validation.json`,
+`review.json`, `task.md`) inside the fixture project, and `sop report [run-id]`
+renders the same run; `sop status` prints task state; `sop approvals --json`
+prints pending approval gates. Run IDs are read from the fixture's
+`.agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/` directory and/or the `sop report`/`sop status` output.
+
+The run script (`scripts/etoe-005-fixture-run.sh`, §3.3) captures these
+deterministically and appends them to `<fixture-root>/etoe-005-run-records.txt`
+in the format:
+
+```text
+# format: <task> | <run-id> | <observed outcome> | <surface>
+FIX-SUCCESS | <run-id> | <outcome> | .agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/state.json + sop report
+FIX-FAIL    | <run-id> | <outcome> | .agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/state.json + sop report
+FIX-GATE    | <run-id> | <outcome> | .agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/state.json + sop approvals --json
+```
+
+### 5.1 Run-record status
+
+> **Execution status.** The governed implementation harness is repository-root
+> confined and cannot execute a separate project under `/tmp/etoe-005-fixture`;
+> executing the fixture project's runs is an operator-run step performed outside
+> the harness (see §7). This report therefore records the fixture's **predeclared**
+> outcomes and the exact, scripted capture procedure an operator uses to obtain
+> run IDs verbatim. Concrete run-ID values are produced by running
+> `scripts/etoe-005-fixture-run.sh` and reading
+> `<fixture-root>/etoe-005-run-records.txt`. No run-ID value is fabricated here;
+> where a value is not observed it is recorded as `UNAVAILABLE` with the reason.
+
+| Task          | Input                     | Expected outcome (predeclared)                | Run ID                                          | Observed outcome                                | Observation surface                       |
+| ------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
+| `FIX-SUCCESS` | `tasks/FIX-SUCCESS.md`    | `completed` / `LOCAL_DONE`, validation PASS    | `PENDING` — captured by `etoe-005-fixture-run.sh` | `PENDING` — same | `.agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/state.json`, `sop report`, `sop status` |
+| `FIX-FAIL`    | `tasks/FIX-FAIL.md`       | validation FAIL / `BLOCKED`                   | `PENDING` — captured by `etoe-005-fixture-run.sh` | `PENDING` — same | `.agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/state.json`, `sop report` |
+| `FIX-GATE`    | `tasks/FIX-GATE.md`       | `needs_human` gate / approval request         | `PENDING` — captured by `etoe-005-fixture-run.sh` | `PENDING` — same | `.agent-sdlc/runs/<id>/state.json`, `sop approvals --json` |
+
+Run-ID capture for the first execution is a single reproducible command (§3.3 /
+§8). Because creation, execution, capture, and teardown are all scripted and
+parameterized by the fixture root and binary, a reader can reproduce the baseline
+and obtain run IDs into a stable records file without ad-hoc steps.
+
+### 5.2 Teardown execution record
+
+```bash
+scripts/etoe-005-fixture-teardown.sh /tmp/etoe-005-fixture
+# expected: teardown: removed /tmp/etoe-005-fixture
+```
+
+The teardown script reports whether removal succeeded and leaves no fixture
+residue outside the disposable root.
